  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is whether a multimodal pipeline with a pretrained RNA encoder (scgpt) and a standard image encoder (resnet50) provides a strong baseline for cellular profiling. config_001 tests this core hypothesis using the simplest aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (concat), which keeps training cost moderate (two encoders, multiprofile, but no transformer or ViT-L). Establishing this multimodal baseline first lets subsequent experiments isolate the value of more complex aggregation (transformer), stronger encoders (ViT-L, scvi_n200), and alternative fusion (weighted) against a known reference. Expected relative cost: low-to-moderate—cheaper than any config using imagenet_vit_l or transformer aggregation, but more expensive than single-modality or single-profile setups."
}

